# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/der_oracle/ (the shipped pipeline told
# the true number of speakers, on the held-out AMI test split).
#
# Job 8976355 (au_der_oracle), 2026-10-04, account educ-lift, an NVIDIA
# L40S on htc-g070, from the clone ~/paper_speech_transcription_audit_w2 at
# code 9cb43e3 with a clean tree, as its environment record and the
# summary's run_metadata say. The record, environment/au_der_oracle_8976355.txt
# beside the original's results on ARC, gives the effective parameters
# SPLIT=test, MIX_MODE=timeline, CACHE_DIR=${DATA}/ami_cache and
# EXTRA_ARGS=--oracle-num-speakers. Its log,
# logs/benchmark_der_8976355.out in that clone, shows the preflight passing
# with --diarisation-required and the 16 meetings read from the timeline
# cache.
#
# Job 8534775 (2026-08-10, htc-g067, code not recorded) ran these settings
# first; its files are in git at aaffb81. The two runs agree on every
# meeting but EN2002c (audit finding EDER-02, 2bb4224).
#
# CACHE_DIR below is the script's default at 9cb43e3, written out so that a
# later change of the default cannot change what this record reproduces.
# The other variables the script turns into arguments are set empty: sbatch
# passes the submitting shell's variables through, and a value left there
# would otherwise reach the job.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC), on the card type the
# original ran on:
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/der_oracle.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-lift --gres=gpu:l40s:1 hpc/submit_benchmark_der.sh )
#
# A reproduction writes to its own directory under repro/, so it cannot
# overwrite the ARC copy of the original run it is to be compared with.
# original: REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/der/der_oracle"
SPLIT=test
MIX_MODE=timeline
CACHE_DIR="${DATA}/ami_cache"
LIMIT_MEETINGS=
MAX_MINUTES=
UTT_PER_MEETING=
CLUSTERING_THRESHOLD=
MIN_CLUSTER_SIZE=
MIN_DURATION_OFF=
SEGMENTATION_MODEL=
ORACLE_NUM_SPEAKERS=1
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/der_oracle"
